n","Yanping Zhong","Wei Cheng","Zhihong Xue","Haiyan Ren"],"published":"2026-09-03","year":2026,"month":9,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-77439-7","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7206163851","title":"Model-free pattern separation of two-color ultrafast X-ray diffraction","authors":["Linos Hecht","Yevheniy Ovcharenko","Asbjørn Ø. Lægdsmand","Björn Bastian","Th. Baumann","Alessandro Colombo","Subhendu De","A. De Fanis","Simon Dold","Thomas Fennel","Robert Hartmann","Katharina Kolatzki","Sivarama Krishnan","Björn Kruse","Aaron LaForge","Bruno Langbehn","S. Mandal","Tommaso Mazza","C. Medina","Christian Peltz","Thomas Pfeifer","Björn Senfftleben","Keshav Sishodia","F. Stienkemeier","Rico Mayro P. Tanyag","Paul Tuemmler","Sergey Usenko","Andreas Heidenreich","Michael Meyer","Daniela Rupp","M. Mudrich"],"published":"2026-09-02","year":2026,"month":9,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-77085-z","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":["MedImg","HealthMon"],"_topics":["ultrafast x-ray diffraction","pattern separation","free electron laser"],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0,"summary_zh":"研究通过使用不同光子能量的X射线脉冲，实现了两色超快X射线衍射的无模型模式分离。利用高能光子脉冲的优势，实现了纳米尺度粒子的结构动态研究。","summary_en":"This study achieves model-free pattern separation in two-color ultrafast X-ray diffraction using X-ray pulses of different photon energies. It takes advantage of high-energy photon pulses to study ultrafast structural dynamics in nanoscale particles.","insights":["创新点：无模型模式分离两色超快X射线衍射","方法亮点：利用高能光子脉冲","关键发现：研究纳米尺度粒子的结构动态"],"insights_en":["Novelty: Model-free pattern separation in two-color ultrafast X-ray diffraction","Method highlight: Utilizing high-energy photon pulses","Key finding: Studying ultrafast structural dynamics in nanoscale particles"],"abstract":"Abstract Two-color X-ray imaging with Free Electron Laser pulses offers a powerful approach for probing ultrafast structural dynamics in nanoscale systems, combining (near-)atomic spatial resolution with femtosecond temporal precision. The first X-ray pulse captures the object’s initial state, while the second, time-delayed pulse records its subsequent evolution. A key challenge lies in disentangling the two patterns simultaneously recorded by the same detector. We demonstrate the realization of this approach on structurally varying nanoscale particles using two X-ray pulses of different photon energies, 1 and 1.2 keV. Sub-micrometer helium nanodroplets generated in vacuum are irradiated by the two X-ray pulses separated in time by up to 750 femtoseconds. Taking advantage of the high photon-energy resolution of the imaging detector, we separate the overlapping diffraction signals by analyzing individual pixel counts and applying pattern recognition. The helium nanodroplets’ spherical shape allows us to cross-validate this approach by fitting the radial scattering profiles with Mie solutions for abichromatic field. The excellent agreement between the two methods, particularly in the sparsely illuminated outer regions of the diffraction patterns where high-resolution structural information is encoded, highlights the quality of this approach and its potential for future advanced X-ray movie techniques."},{"id":"openalex:W7206186143","title":"Interfacial spin-order engineering mitigates the permeability-loss trade-off in amorphous soft magnetic composites","authors":["Huaping Ding","Shengxiang Wang","Jie Chen","Fei Hu","Liliang Shao","Haibo Ke","Pan Gong","Congrui Yang","Jiyu Xu","Yuqiang Yan","Jing Zhou","Xing Tong","Xinyun Wang","Weihua Wang"],"published":"2026-09-02","year":2026,"month":9,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-77457-5","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7206186306","title":"Photon-driven magnetization switching in Fe₃GeTe₂ enables programmable, multilevel magnetic memory","authors":["Wei-Qing Li","Sheng-Hsiung Hung","Jia-Xin Li","Chung-Chun Lu","Po‐Liang Chen","Ching Kuo","Kun-Hung Pan","Horng‐Tay Jeng","Chang‐Hua Liu"],"published":"2026-09-02","year":2026,"month":9,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-77178-9","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0}]